          <h2 class="section-title" id="about-project-heading">About Neminath One Reserve, Borivali West by Neminath</h2>
          
<div class="description-content-box">
  <div class="desc-text"><p>Neminath One Reserve is a residential project in Borivali West, Mumbai. It is planned as a small, private residential setup. The idea is to keep daily living calm and well-organized.</p><p>Borivali West is a well-known and well-used residential area. Getting around from here is fairly easy. Main roads, markets, schools, and hospitals are close by. Public transport options are also available nearby. This helps residents manage daily travel without much effort.</p><p>The project is built on a land parcel of around 0.33 acres. Neminath One Reserve consists of two residential towers. The project offers both 2 and 3 bedroom homes. Apartment sizes range from 242 sq ft to 1026 sq ft. There are only 50 homes in total, which results in privacy and quiet surroundings.</p><p>Homes are planned with everyday use in mind. Room shapes are simple and easy to furnish. Windows allow daylight and fresh air to move through the spaces. Everything feels practical rather than decorative.</p><p>Shared areas are meant for regular daily use. There is a central green space where residents can step out. Kids have a dedicated play area within the premises. Jogging tracks support daily walks and light exercise. Yoga areas are kept aside for calm routines. Indoor game spaces add a simple recreation option. Retail outlets within the project help with daily needs.</p><p>Neminath One Reserve is developed by Neminath. The developer has over 27 years of experience in real estate. Their work usually focuses on simple layouts and clear planning. This project follows the same straightforward approach.</p><p><strong>Location Advantages of Neminath One Reserve, Borivali West, Mumbai</strong></p><p>Neminath One Reserve in Borivali West, Mumbai, enjoys a prime address with great connectivity to key transport routes and easy access to everyday conveniences.</p><p><strong>Key Destinations:</strong>&nbsp; </p><ul><li>Borivali Railway Station – 2 Km</li><li>Western Express Highway – 15 mins&nbsp;</li><li>Mumbai International Airport – 15 mins</li><li>S.V. Road: less than 5 mins</li></ul><p><strong>Proximity to Business and IT Hubs: </strong></p><p>Nirlon Knowledge Park, NESCO IT Park, Mindspace Malad, Infinity IT Park, Techno Park</p><p><strong>Social Infrastructure:&nbsp;</strong></p><p> The neighbourhood is well-developed and offers all essential conveniences close by.</p><ul><li><strong>Shopping &amp; Entertainment:</strong> Zone Mall, Croma Mall, Reliance Mall</li><li><strong>Healthcare: </strong>Rajendra Nursing Home, Shri Adinath Digamber Jain Chikitsalaya</li><li><strong>Education: </strong>Don Bosco High School, Sai Lee International School</li></ul><p><strong>Upcoming Infrastructure Near Neminath One Reserve, Borivali West, Mumbai</strong></p><ul><li>The Thane–Borivali Tunnel will reduce travel time from nearly two hours to about 15 minutes.</li><li>The Mumbai Road Project will improve road connectivity from South Mumbai to Dahisar.</li><li>Metro Line 2A will make daily travel across the western suburbs more convenient.</li><li>The Goregaon–Mulund Link Road (GMLR) will enhance east–west connectivity across the city.</li></ul><p><strong>Neminath One Reserve, Borivali West, Mumbai: An Investment Marvel </strong></p><p>Mumbai has emerged as a prime location for those who seek an urban lifestyle with modern conveniences.</p><ul><li>Borivali West has seen a steady price growth of around 1.21%* in the past year.</li><li>Average rental returns in the area are close to 3%*.</li><li>The locality is well connected to both railway and metro stations.</li></ul><p><em>*These figures are derived from our Data Intelligence team and may differ slightly in actuality.*</em></p><p> Neminath One Reserve is a practical residential choice for buyers seeking calm living with strong Borivali West connectivity.&nbsp;</p></div>
  <div class="read-more-button-box">
    <button type="button" class="read-more-button global-read-more-btn" aria-expanded="false">Read More</button>
  </div>
</div>

      </section>



      
